// Two segments overlap if they share any interior point. Segments [i,j] and [k,l] overlap if max(i,k) < min(j,l).
// They can touch at endpoints, so [i,j] and [j,l] do NOT overlap.
//
// This is equivalent to finding the maximum number of segments that all pairwise overlap (i.e., have a common interior point).
