// For intervals, the maximum clique is the maximum number of intervals that all share a common point.
//
// For segments [i, j] with integer endpoints, two segments overlap if they share at least one interior point.
// Actually, let's think more carefully. Two segments [a,b] and [c,d] overlap (in the sense that they cannot be in the same layer) if their intersection has positive length, i.e., max(a,c) < min(b,d).
